# ControlCentre blocks for the VATSSA VPS Caddyfile.
#
# Path is /srv/deploy/caddy/conf/Caddyfile — NOT /srv/deploy/caddy/Caddyfile,
# which older docs still say.
#
# Apply with:
#   docker exec caddy caddy validate --config /etc/caddy/Caddyfile
#   cd /srv/deploy/caddy && docker compose restart
#
# `caddy reload` is DISABLED on this box: the global block sets `admin off`,
# which kills the admin API reload depends on. A restart briefly drops every
# site, so never do it during an event.
#
# Three things here are specific to this box and easy to get wrong:
#
#  1. `http://` prefixes. TLS terminates at Cloudflare and cloudflared speaks
#     plain HTTP to Caddy, and the global block sets `auto_https off`. A bare
#     hostname would make Caddy attempt its own ACME certificate, which cannot
#     succeed here.
#
#  2. `security_headers_livewire`, not `security_headers`. CC v7.0.0 is
#     Livewire 4 + Flux, and Alpine uses new Function(), so script-src needs
#     'unsafe-eval'. The plain snippet omits it and CSP blocks the JS silently
#     — role assignment included. This was correct for v6.4.3, which had no
#     Livewire; the upgrade changed the requirement.
#
#  3. `header_up X-Forwarded-Proto https`. Without it Laravel behind the tunnel
#     generates http:// URLs and can loop on secure-cookie redirects.
#
# cc.vatssa.com is defined here even before the production cutover. That is
# safe: there is no Cloudflare Tunnel public hostname for it, so nothing
# outside can reach it. Adding that hostname IS the cutover.

# ── ControlCentre ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
http://cc.vatssa.com {
  import security_headers_livewire
  reverse_proxy cc-prod:80 {
    header_up X-Forwarded-Proto https
  }
  log {
    output file /var/log/caddy/cc-prod.log
  }
}

http://cc-staging.vatssa.com {
  import security_headers_livewire
  reverse_proxy cc-staging:80 {
    header_up X-Forwarded-Proto https
  }
  log {
    output file /var/log/caddy/cc-staging.log
  }
}

http://cc-dev.vatssa.com {
  import security_headers_livewire
  reverse_proxy cc-dev:80 {
    header_up X-Forwarded-Proto https
  }
  log {
    output file /var/log/caddy/cc-dev.log
  }
}
